 ### SplineSplat
-Computes tomographic projections of a volume represented by a linear combination of shifted B-splines [S7]. Sets itself apart from standard DDA by extending traversal to handle overlapping, compactly supported basis functions using a neural network to compute basis contributions, avoiding closed-form analytical expressions [S7]. Choose it for higher-quality tomographic reconstruction where traditional voxel-based methods lack precision [S7].
+SplineSplat is a 3D ray-tracing algorithm that computes tomographic projections of a volume represented by a linear combination of shifted B-splines. It extends DDA to handle overlapping, compactly supported basis functions by using a neural network to compute basis contributions, avoiding the need for closed-form analytical expressions [S6].
